// 1543:3
[com_3]
type=text
y=5
width=10
height=32
widthmode=minus
xmode=abs_centre
layer=com_2
textfont=fontmetrics_26
fontmono=no
text=<col=aed0e0>General Rewards: </col>You can use both event points and trophies to purchase reward lamps. Points are gained by dismissing ghosts. Trophies are given once a day when you participate in dismissing a demonic ghost. Trophies can also be used to purchase the Ghost Hunter title and Proto Pack emote. The title is available through the Title tab on your Wardrobe interface.
textshadow=yes
colour=0x7592a0

// 1543:4
[com_4]
type=text
y=67
width=10
height=32
widthmode=minus
xmode=abs_centre
layer=com_2
textfont=fontmetrics_26
fontmono=no
text=<col=aed0e0>Ghost Hunter Gear: </col>The ghost hunter costume will scale to your level as hybrid armour. It begins at level 20 and improves at 50 and 70. Each item you wear also gives bonus damage versus spirits and ghosts - specifically any creature that gives Prayer XP through an ectoplasmator. You also gain bonus XP for killing these monsters. The bonus increases for each part of the set you are wearing.
textshadow=yes
colour=0x7592a0

// 1543:5
[com_5]
type=text
y=129
width=10
height=32
widthmode=minus
xmode=abs_centre
layer=com_2
textfont=fontmetrics_26
fontmono=no
text=<col=aed0e0>Cremation Ability: </col>With this ability unlocked you will be able to burn bones in fires. You still need to light a fire before you can begin! Adding bones works like adding logs and can provide a boost to health. The XP gained will be given in Firemaking at the rate of double the bones' Prayer XP. You will also gain 250% of the Prayer XP you would gain for burying the bones normally.
textshadow=yes
colour=0x7592a0

// 1543:6
[com_6]
type=text
y=194
width=10
height=32
widthmode=minus
xmode=abs_centre
layer=com_2
textfont=fontmetrics_26
fontmono=no
text=<col=aed0e0>Proto Pack Cosmetic Override: </col>For dismissing 50 ghosts in the house you will unlock the proto pack as a cosmetic override for daggers, claws and crossbows. When used as a crossbow the item will replace the projectile you are using with blasts of science-tastic energy. This is purely a cosmetic effect. The items are available in your Wardrobe interface when you have unlocked them.
textshadow=yes
colour=0x7592a0

